Input The live <code>document</code> of a rendered page, plus an optional configuration object (<code>framework</code>, <code>stageWidth</code>, <code>stageHeight</code>, <code>breaks</code>). Processing <code>preprocess()</code> collects background colours from the page's stylesheets, removes page chrome (navigation, headers, footers, sidebars), picks or builds one <code>&lt;section&gt;</code> per slide, and classifies each slide's layout and background. Output The same <code>document</code>, mutated in place so that <code>&lt;body&gt;</code> contains only the slide sections, and an object <code>{ html }</code> that holds <code>document.documentElement.outerHTML</code>. <pre><code>import { preprocess } from "vexy-dexyjs";

const { html } = preprocess({ framework: "generic" });
// document.body now holds &lt;section class="slide ..."&gt; elements only.
</code></pre> <p>The output is framework-neutral. It is not shaped for reveal.js specifically, so the same DOM can feed reveal.js, impress.js or CSS paged media.</p>
